{
  "methodology": "Four live CPU Rep4 Party roles over IdealNetwork, exact floor truncation. Global bytes sum all outgoing payloads, including runtime consistency hashes. Inputs are already shared; witness input and all domain/residual verification and accept-bit opening are included. Final output opening is excluded for every mode. Witnesses use nearest reciprocal of the independently reproducible encoded denominator. References use torch float64 on encoded input fixtures. These are activation-level accuracy and communication measurements, not model accuracy or distributed latency. Numerical baselines retain caller-established domains; the witness path includes private domain checks. Polynomial denotes existing degree-ten FixedPoint methods; numerical denotes the more accurate NumericalFixedPoint formulas. Mixed polynomial uses the selected mixed degree-eight SiLU or degree-ten GELU schedule in ring32/Q14 with caller-established input bounds; its precision and range-check policy differ.",
